1
00:01:18,947 --> 00:01:24,947
The world’s first Easter egg hunt. It all started right here.

2
00:02:37,894 --> 00:02:43,894
Ice Age: The Great Egg-Scapade is a adventure, animation,
comedy film directed by Ricardo Curtis.

3
00:03:56,842 --> 00:04:02,842
A harried prehistoric bird mother entrusts her
precious, soon-to-hatch egg to Sid.

4
00:05:15,789 --> 00:05:21,789
When she recommends him to her neighbours, business
booms at his new egg-sitting service.

5
00:06:34,736 --> 00:06:40,736
However, dastardly pirate bunny, Squint, who is seeking revenge on
the herd, steals, camouflages and hides all the eggs.

6
00:07:53,684 --> 00:07:59,684
Once again, with Squint’s twin brother assisting, Manny, Diego and the rest of the gang come to the
rescue and take off on a daring mission that turns into the world’s first Easter egg hunt.

7
00:09:12,631 --> 00:09:18,631
Manny (voice), played by Ray Romano.

8
00:10:31,578 --> 00:10:37,578
Sid (voice), played by John Leguizamo.

9
00:11:50,526 --> 00:11:56,526
Diego (voice), played by Denis Leary.

10
00:13:09,473 --> 00:13:15,473
Ethel (voice), played by Taraji P. Henson.

11
00:14:28,421 --> 00:14:34,421
Ellie (voice), played by Queen Latifah.

12
00:15:47,368 --> 00:15:53,368
Cholly Bear (voice), played by Gabriel Iglesias.

13
00:17:06,315 --> 00:17:12,315
Ice Age: The Great Egg-Scapade is a 2016 animated comedy-mystery television
special, produced by Blue Sky Studios and directed by Ricardo Curtis.

14
00:18:25,263 --> 00:18:31,263
It premiered on Fox during the Easter season.

15
00:19:44,210 --> 00:19:50,210
Most of the actors reprise their roles from the previous installments except
Aziz Ansari, whose role as Squint was replaced by Seth Green.

16
00:21:03,157 --> 00:21:09,157
It takes place between Ice Age: Continental Drift and Ice Age: Collision Course.

17
00:22:22,105 --> 00:22:28,105
The film explores themes of squirrel, mammoth, ice age, easter, prehistory.

18
00:23:41,052 --> 00:23:47,052
The tone is lighthearted.
